     "text": "{\"count\": 0, \"rationale\": \"No single step is a chokepoint. The target is an OR of four branches (shareMount, vaultRead, dbReplica, codeRepo), and every candidate leaves at least one branch reachable. shareMount alone has redundant parents: backupHost, reachable via apiToken or via ssoLogin, and printServer, reachable via tokenCache. tokenCache in turn is fed by three independent parents (iotDevice, the vpnGateway foothold, workstation). Blocking tokenCache removes printServer and apiToken, but backupHost stays reachable through ssoLogin (iotDevice AND memoryDump, both reachable). Blocking backupHost leaves printServer. Blocking ssoLogin leaves apiToken (dmzWeb AND tokenCache). The dbReplica branch (via domainAdmin = fileServer AND dbLogin) also remains independently reachable. So no single blocked step makes crownData:exfiltrate unreachable.\"}"
    }
